  "title": "Shang dynasty",
  "summary": "The Shang dynasty ruled in the Yellow River region of China from about 1600 to 1046 BCE. Its late capital at Yin, near modern Anyang, is confirmed by oracle bone inscriptions and excavation as the first site of a capital in Chinese history. Those inscriptions, used in divination, are the earliest known mature writing in China. Shang foundries cast bronze on a large scale. King Wu of Zhou overthrew the dynasty at the Battle of Muye in 1046 BCE.",
